{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לך לך", :translit "lekh lekha", :gloss "Go, you"} {:he "מאמר", :translit "ma'amar", :gloss "utterance"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word מאמר links Abraham's call to the ten utterances of creation"}], :frame {:text "The world was created by ten utterances (Pirkei Avot 5:1). All of it was created only for the merit of Abraham, as stated: 'On that day HaShem cut a covenant with Abram' (Genesis 15:18) is interpreted to mean the world was created for his sake (Bereishit Rabbah 12:9, Shabbat 10a records that HaShem's very name is only recalled for the patriarchs). Therefore the divine address to Abraham is fittingly framed as a מאמר, an utterance paralleling the utterances by which the world was brought into being.", :sources ["Pirkei Avot 5:1" "Genesis 15:18" "Bereishit Rabbah 12:9" "Shabbat 10a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לך לך", :translit "lekha lekha", :gloss "to you, to you"} {:he "ואעשך לגוי גדול", :translit "ve'e'eskha le-goy gadol", :gloss "and I will make you a great nation"} {:he "לך", :translit "lekh", :gloss "go / for you"} {:he "בחרן", :translit "be-kharan", :gloss "in Haran"} {:he "חרון אף", :translit "kharon af", :gloss "burning anger"} {:he "ויהי בחרן", :translit "vayehi be-kharan", :gloss "and it was in Haran"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לך לך", :b "מאה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "לך לך", :b "עה"} {:kind :gematria, :a "לך", :b "נ"} {:kind :other, :note "Two occurrences of לך hint to two exiles"} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "חרון אף", :spells "חרן"}], :frame {:text "Isaac was born to Abraham at age one hundred (Genesis 21:5). Abraham departed Haran at age seventy-five and lived to one hundred seventy-five (Genesis 12:4, 25:7). The covenant between the pieces foresaw exile for Abraham's descendants (Genesis 15:13–14). That passage states the exile would last four hundred years counted from Isaac's birth; the southern kingdom's exile under Zedekiah is recorded in II Kings 25:1–21.", :sources ["G